    "sourceWikitext": "{{recipesummary|category=Caribbean recipes |servings=4|time=45 minutes|difficulty=2}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine|Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Caribbean cuisines|Caribbean cuisines]] | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Trinidad and Tobago|Cuisine of Trinidad and Tobago]]\n\n'''Chinese chews''' are a bar [[Cookbook:Cookie|cookie]] containing nuts and dried fruit. They have a chewy consistency.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]s\n*⅔ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*⅔ cup [[Cookbook:Self-rising Flour|self-raising flour]]\n*⅓ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]]\n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Date|dates]]\n*½ cup seedless [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisin]]s\n*¾ cup chopped [[Cookbook:Walnut|walnut]]s\n*[[Cookbook:Confectioners' sugar|Icing sugar]] to taste\n\n==Procedure==\n#[[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] eggs until foamy. Add sugar and mix.\n#Add flour and salt.\n#Add vanilla, then the fruit and nuts. Mix well.\n#Spread in greased 8-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] [[Cookbook:Cake Pan|cake pan]].\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for about 30–35 minutes at 350°F (175°C) until golden brown.\n#Cut into squares while still warm. Roll in icing sugar.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n*Can be enjoyed on its own or with ice cream.\n*Cools to a firm consistency.\n\n[[Category:Caribbean recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using date]]\n[[Category:Recipes using walnut]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using self-raising flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes for cookies]]",
